WEBVTT

00:00.740 --> 00:02.386
On the 29th of October,

00:02.386 --> 00:07.540
attackers drained $6.3 billion from
Binance's hot wallets in one attack.

00:07.580 --> 00:10.528
It is the largest crypto theft on record,

00:10.528 --> 00:13.980
attributed to North Korea's TraderTraitor
group.

00:14.020 --> 00:18.620
The keys sat on internet-connected machines,
and they got taken.

00:18.660 --> 00:27.270
It isn't alone. In 2026 so far, over 8
billion has been stolen in over 300 hacks.

00:27.310 --> 00:30.440
It's a record year, with a month still to
go.

00:30.740 --> 00:36.740
If the biggest exchange can't keep online
keys safe, neither can a browser extension.

00:36.780 --> 00:39.260
The only safe key is the offline key.

00:41.863 --> 00:44.593
And even the hardware wallets have a weak
spot:

00:44.633 --> 00:46.093
the box they ship in.

00:46.133 --> 00:47.161
In October 2026,

00:47.161 --> 00:51.593
Ledger devices sold by reseller CryptoBilis
carried a hidden implant.

00:51.633 --> 00:56.793
It read the 24 words off the screen and sent
them out over the mobile network.

00:56.833 --> 01:02.093
Between $86 and $93 million was stolen.

01:02.133 --> 01:04.293
And Ledger's Genuine Check couldn't catch
it.

01:04.333 --> 01:06.293
It checks only the secure chip.

01:06.333 --> 01:09.833
With Bunker, there is no device in the mail
to intercept.

01:11.350 --> 01:13.950
So what is the solution? Go offline.

01:13.990 --> 01:18.800
Bunker turns the old Android phone in your
drawer into a hardware wallet.

01:19.080 --> 01:20.900
Any phone with Android 8 or newer works.

01:21.460 --> 01:23.570
No new device to buy or ship.

01:23.610 --> 01:29.310
Seal it. With airplane mode on, Wi-Fi,
Bluetooth and NFC off.

01:29.350 --> 01:32.190
The app has no internet permissions at all.

01:32.230 --> 01:36.060
Bunker's banner turns from Exposed to
Bunker.

01:38.810 --> 01:42.140
So how does it work? There are two QR codes:
no cable, no Bluetooth, no network.

01:42.180 --> 01:44.610
You need a wallet, like MetaMask or Rabby.

01:44.610 --> 01:49.180
It builds the raw transaction and shows it
as an animated QR code to the phone.

01:49.220 --> 01:52.100
You scan it with the phone and decode it.

01:52.540 --> 01:57.840
It decodes it on the device for you to read
the amount, where it's sent, and the fee.

01:57.880 --> 02:01.200
Then you approve it with your fingerprint or
PIN code, and the phone signs it.

02:01.240 --> 02:05.060
After that, you show the QR code back to
your device's camera.

02:05.850 --> 02:07.860
Then you just need to broadcast the
transaction.

02:07.900 --> 02:12.040
The recovery phrase on your phone never
leaves. It's always there.

02:13.497 --> 02:14.357
Clear signing.

02:14.397 --> 02:18.497
Blind signing is how most wallet drains
happen. Bunker never does that.

02:18.537 --> 02:22.447
It decodes every transaction on the phone,
and computes what gets signed itself.

02:22.487 --> 02:26.605
Every argument of a contract call is shown.
Unknown tokens,

02:26.605 --> 02:29.817
unlimited approvals and high fees are
flagged.

02:29.857 --> 02:33.849
Anything it can't show in full is refused,
and never blind-signed.

02:33.849 --> 02:35.967
That's the only way to stay secure.

02:36.007 --> 02:42.028
It covers BNB and BEP-20 transfers, and
swaps on KyberSwap,

02:42.028 --> 02:46.927
Velora and 1inch via the open ERC-7730
registry,

02:46.967 --> 02:50.007
and Ondo and xStocks tokenized stocks.

02:51.353 --> 02:52.267
Hardware-sealed seed.

02:52.267 --> 02:55.573
The recovery phrase is encrypted under a key
in the phone's secure hardware:

02:55.823 --> 02:59.353
StrongBox or the TEE, as long as your phone
supports this.

02:59.393 --> 03:01.433
Each signature needs your fingerprint or
PIN.

03:01.883 --> 03:04.818
The best is Pixel 8 or newer with
GrapheneOS: Titan M2 chip,

03:04.818 --> 03:06.433
memory tagging and a hardened OS.

03:07.433 --> 03:12.313
Anything from Pixel 6 or later, where the
Titan M2 holds the seed key, is great.

03:12.923 --> 03:15.771
And if you are not afraid of a physical
attack,

03:15.771 --> 03:18.073
any old Android phone is totally fine.

03:18.113 --> 03:20.013
They keep you offline and secure.

03:20.053 --> 03:21.718
Every QR is treated as an attack,

03:21.718 --> 03:24.493
and the code is open source under the Apache
2 license.

03:25.930 --> 03:27.680
And what is the challenging part?

03:27.720 --> 03:30.320
Well, clear signing only works if it's up to
date,

03:30.360 --> 03:33.440
and an offline device is really hard to
update.

03:33.480 --> 03:35.632
We don't have this feature yet,

03:35.632 --> 03:39.520
but in the future we're going to enable QR
code updates.

03:39.560 --> 03:43.286
So by scanning, like, hundreds of QR codes,

03:43.286 --> 03:47.360
we plan to bring the phone's runtime up to
date

03:47.400 --> 03:49.840
to support all the changes in the DEXs.

03:49.880 --> 03:55.700
So there is no need to reinstall the whole
phone again when you need to update.

03:57.140 --> 04:02.960
Why now? Over 700 tokenized stocks and ETFs
trade 24/7 on BNB Chain.

04:03.000 --> 04:08.960
Ondo, xStocks and Binance's own bStocks
bring real-world equities on-chain.

04:09.000 --> 04:12.072
People holding their portfolio in
self-custody need

04:12.072 --> 04:14.000
a vault that is safe and simple.

04:17.176 --> 04:19.026
So, what does the roadmap look like?

04:19.066 --> 04:22.207
The signing core and Android app are built,

04:22.207 --> 04:27.026
and I have done my security review on the
code, and initial fixes.

04:27.066 --> 04:33.546
There is a testnet beta, and there are
backups for SLIP-39 and even Banana Split,

04:33.546 --> 04:36.026
to split your 24-word mnemonic.

04:36.066 --> 04:41.246
What is planned next? The first release,
distributed on F-Droid and GitHub.

04:41.286 --> 04:47.066
And if we get funded, hopefully external
audits and a bug bounty will be in place.

04:47.176 --> 04:50.686
And in the longer term, the core work has to
be on updatability.

04:52.076 --> 04:55.366
So: an old phone, airplane mode, MetaMask
over QR codes.

04:56.586 --> 04:57.686
Keep your keys bunkered.

04:57.726 --> 05:01.666
Visit bunker.rotko.net for the initial
release.
